title: The pacer checks Jeff's files after every session it starts, and what to read is in 'data/claude/pacer/jeff-check.log'.
pid: e9b7f23b-cc0e-4994-bf0a-cb6813ec1d9c
body: |2-
  Built 2026-11-14 at Libby's asking; her procedure for reading what the
  check finds is in her graph, under "I check that nothing of ours
  changed a file of Jeff's ...". The script is
  'tools/team/check_jeffs_files.py'; its docstring and the pacer's
  header ("THE CHECK OF JEFF'S FILES") say what each step does.
  In the log, each window is one line of counts, from a session the
  pacer started ('session STAMP'), the daily check ('day') or a run by
  hand; the indented lines under it are the ones to read: OURS?,
  UNPLACED, STAGED, GONE, a deletion count his server does not explain,
  and our tool calls that may write. A window with none is clean.
  'specialist.sh' writes its own line there each time it writes Jeff's
  config, and the check reads those lines to place the write.
contains:
- 1323dfe1-861e-449d-9721-af87fdc17195
- 5d568c80-125b-497c-b5e6-bf574d9a6a66
- 39c93b4c-99b3-40bb-b661-19c0953827e0
